%% How one request is judged - the private endpoint path versus the public endpoint firewall, with the 403 failure branch that a lock-down produces
%% Source: Microsoft Learn - Azure Storage firewall rules and network access; Networking considerations for Azure Files (portal file browser 403, CallerIpAddress); Trusted Azure services (Microsoft.StorageSync); Back up Azure Files FAQ (Azure Backup uses key-based access); codex/runbook-file-sync-broken-after-network-lockdown.md classes 1, 2 and 4
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant SRV as Contoso file server
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant PE as Private endpoint NIC 10.51.x.x
  participant SA as Storage account data plane
  participant FWL as Storage firewall on the public endpoint
  participant SSS as Storage Sync Service
  participant BK as Azure Backup
  participant ADM as Administrator browser

  Note over SRV,SA: Path A - the private path Contoso is paying ExpressRoute for
  SRV->>IB: account.file.core.windows.net ?
  IB-->>SRV: CNAME to account.privatelink.file.core.windows.net then A 10.51.x.x
  SRV->>PE: TCP 445 SMB, or TCP 443 FileREST, over private peering
  PE->>SA: forwarded on the Microsoft backbone
  SA-->>SRV: served. The public-endpoint firewall rules were never consulted on this path
  Note over PE,SA: Authorisation on this path is the approved private-link connection plus Kerberos or the account key. Network rules govern the public endpoint only

  Note over SRV,FWL: Path B - the same request when DNS was never forwarded
  SRV->>IB: account.file.core.windows.net ?
  IB-->>SRV: A 52.239.x.x - the public storage cluster, because no privatelink forwarder exists
  SRV->>FWL: TCP 445 from Contoso public egress IP
  alt defaultAction is still Allow
    FWL-->>SRV: served over the internet path. Silent failure - the traffic left the circuit and nobody noticed
  else defaultAction Deny with no matching IP rule
    FWL-->>SRV: 403
    SRV->>SRV: Telemetry 9102 with a non-zero HResult, recall errors 9006, server endpoint turns Error
    Note over SRV,FWL: Recovery - add the Infoblox forwarder, Clear-DnsClientCache, or temporarily add the egress IP as an IP rule
  end

  Note over SSS,FWL: Path C - the leg Microsoft initiates and you cannot move
  SSS->>FWL: cloud change enumeration and cloud endpoint operations against the public endpoint
  alt bypass contains AzureServices
    FWL-->>SSS: allowed as a trusted service, resource provider Microsoft.StorageSync
  else bypass was removed, or publicNetworkAccess was set to Disabled
    FWL-->>SSS: rejected
    Note over SSS,FWL: Server sync sessions may keep running while change enumeration silently never completes. Assessor AFS-14 or SEC-05
  end

  Note over BK,FWL: Path D - Azure Backup for Azure file shares
  BK->>FWL: snapshot and restore operations on the same storage account
  alt allowSharedKeyAccess true and bypass AzureServices
    FWL-->>BK: allowed. The snapshot stays in this storage account - zero bytes cross a network
  else shared key access disabled
    FWL-->>BK: rejected. Backup jobs fail even though the network rules are correct
  end

  Note over ADM,FWL: Path E - the portal file browser
  ADM->>FWL: direct browser request to the data-plane endpoint with a portal SAS
  alt the browser egress IP is an IP rule
    FWL-->>ADM: file list rendered
  else no IP rule
    FWL-->>ADM: 403 on the data plane while portal.azure.com itself loads normally
    Note over ADM,FWL: Confirm the real source with storage resource logs, field CallerIpAddress, not with the address in the error
  end
